# Supabase (Project Settings → API). Copy to .env.local — never commit secrets.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_ANON_PUBLIC_KEY
# Optional, and preferred when set: Supabase's newer publishable key (sb_publishable_…). Both are PUBLIC keys.
# Never put a service_role or sb_secret_ key in any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable: the build refuses (src/lib/supabase/key-guard.ts).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Profile avatar/banner uploads use the public Storage bucket `profiles`. Resume / portfolio uploads use the
# PRIVATE bucket `resumes` (service role only; served via GET /api/resume/<key> with short-lived signed URLs).
# `profiles` writes are server-only too: owner INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE storage policies were dropped by 20260904110000,
# so uploads go through /api/me/profile-upload + /api/me/profile-sync (service role) — never the Storage REST API.
# If uploads fail with “Bucket not found”, apply migrations to the linked project (`npx supabase link` then
# `npx supabase db push`) or run these in Supabase Dashboard → SQL Editor:
#   supabase/migrations/20260503120000_profile_extension_storage.sql   (profiles)
#   supabase/migrations/20260904100000_private_resumes_bucket.sql      (resumes)
# Server-only — Auth admin (password reset links), school email updates. Never expose to the browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=YOUR_SERVICE_ROLE_SECRET_KEY

# The "are you a person" box (Cloudflare Turnstile) on sign-up, sign-in and "send a new email". This is the SITE key,
# which is public; the SECRET key goes into Supabase only, never in this file or on Vercel.
# UNSET = no box, no Cloudflare script, no Cloudflare host in the browser code rule, and the three forms work exactly
# as before. Local sign-in needs nothing here. To see the box locally, use one of the TEST site keys Cloudflare
# publishes for local use (they work on localhost and always give the same answer):
#   1x00000000000000000000AA always passes · 2x00000000000000000000AB always fails · 3x00000000000000000000FF asks for a tick
# Production, TO TURN IT ON, IN THIS ORDER:
#   (1) Cloudflare > Turnstile > Add widget: hostname connectvibe.app (that covers www), widget mode MANAGED (Invisible
#       would leave a blank gap in the form, since the box always keeps its room), pre-clearance NO.
#   (2) The real site key here on Vercel, with no quotes, then a new deploy (NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are built in).
#   (3) Check the box shows on the live sign-in and sign-up pages. Then sign in three times and watch the button go from
#       "Checking you're a person…" to "Sign in" each time: once in a phone browser, once inside the iPhone app and
#       once inside the Android app (the apps load the live site, and a store reviewer signs in through that page).
#   (4) Only then Supabase > Authentication > Attack Protection > Captcha, provider Turnstile, with the secret.
#       Step 4 before the box is live and passing in all three places locks people out of sign-in.
# TO TURN IT OFF, the other way round: Supabase's switch FIRST (it is instant), then this key. NEVER remove or change
# this key while Supabase's switch is on: a build without it has no box, so every sign-in, sign-up and new email is
# refused until the switch is off, and reloading the page does not help.
# The why and the rules: src/lib/auth/captcha.ts. Left commented out with no value on purpose: a test key copied to
# production would show a box whose tokens the real secret then refuses.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Public site URL for email links (production). Fallback: VERCEL_URL on Vercel, http://localhost:3000 locally.
# School .edu verification links use the host from your current request when possible, so local dev still gets
# http://localhost:3000 even if this points at production (same Chrome session after clicking the link).
# Use your canonical origin (e.g. https://www.connectvibe.app). Sign-up confirmation links use this so they
# match Supabase Auth → URL Configuration. Add both to Redirect URLs:
#   https://www.connectvibe.app/auth/callback**
#   http://localhost:3000/auth/callback**
# Set Site URL to the same canonical origin.
# Must be a real HTTPS URL (e.g. https://www.connectvibe.app). Do not set this to the text NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-deployment.vercel.app

# HMAC secret for campus email verification tokens (min 16 chars, random).
SCHOOL_EMAIL_VERIFY_SECRET=generate_a_long_random_string_here

# Optional — campus email allowlist for school verification, comma-separated. Subdomains match automatically
# (e.g. @mail.iu.edu). Any other .edu is rejected. Defaults to the IU Indianapolis pilot when unset or blank.
# SCHOOL_EMAIL_DOMAINS=iu.edu,purdue.edu   # narrows only; can never add a domain the code map lacks

# Server-only — the HMAC secret behind the moderation ban list. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_*, never in client code.
# Minimum 32 characters, random (`openssl rand -hex 32`). A suspension or ban is keyed on a scrambled
# email — an HMAC of the canonical address under this value, never the address itself — which is what
# makes a ban survive "delete the account and sign up again".
# TWO KINDS OF KEY, and only one of them bites. The SCHOOL key (from the verified school email) is the
# one with teeth: school-email verification tests it, so a banned address can't be verified onto a new
# account. The PERSONAL key (the login address) is EVIDENCE ONLY — sign-up runs from the browser
# straight to GoTrue, so no Vibe route ever sees an account being created and nothing can refuse a
# banned personal address there. An account that never verified a school email gets no enforceable key
# at all: it can be banned, and the same person can sign up again with the same address the same night.
# UNSET, nothing breaks and nothing is silently weakened: suspending and banning fail closed with 503
# `not_configured` ("Restrictions aren't set up on this deploy yet. Nothing was changed."). LIFTING IS
# DELIBERATELY NOT GATED ON IT — it finds rows by `user_id`, so a missing secret can never strand a
# restricted student on the suspension notice. Reports, the queue, removing content, school verification
# and every student path keep working. So production can ship without it, but moderation can't restrict
# anyone until it is set on Vercel (Production only, Sensitive). Set it there before the first suspension.
# IT CAN NEVER BE ROTATED: every stored key is an HMAC under this value and there is no way back from a
# key to an email, so a new value orphans every restriction ever written. Generate once, keep it, back it up.
# LEFT COMMENTED OUT ON PURPOSE: any placeholder long enough to look like an example is also long enough
# to be accepted, so a copied .env.example would arm restrictions under a secret that lives in the repo —
# and this is the one value that can never be rotated away afterwards. Generate your own, or leave it off.
# RESTRICTION_PEPPER=   # openssl rand -hex 32

# Installable app (PWA). The service worker registers on www.connectvibe.app only; nothing to set in production.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SW_DEV=1 lets it register under `next dev` on localhost — against the LOCAL Supabase copy only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SW_KILL=1 is the kill switch's build flag: set it in Vercel (Production) BEFORE pushing the kill commit
# described in scripts/pwa/sw-killswitch.js. Never leave it set afterwards.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SW_DEV=1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SW_KILL=1

# Store listings: the landing's "Get Vibe on …" links and the /get redirect (iPhone → App Store, Android → Play).
# Leave both UNSET until the listing is live. Unset, the landing shows no store link at all and /get sends phones
# to /campus and computers to /. Each value must be the listing's full URL, starting https://apps.apple.com/ or
# https://play.google.com/, or it is ignored. Public on purpose (they're store links), so nothing secret here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined when the app is BUILT: changing one on Vercel does nothing until the next deploy.
# Left commented out with no value, like RESTRICTION_PEPPER: an example URL would pass the prefix check and
# put a dead store link on the landing.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_STORE_URL=   # https://apps.apple.com/app/id…
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAY_STORE_URL=  # https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=…

# The landing's demo film ("A day on Vibe"): the FOLDER holding vibe-demo-780.mp4 and vibe-demo-390.mp4, under
# exactly those names (Vercel Blob: upload without a random suffix). The film shows real people's photos and this
# repo is public, so it is never committed. Leave it UNSET: every build, `next dev` included, reads the film from
# the Vercel Blob store in src/lib/landing/demo-media.ts (DEFAULT_DEMO_MEDIA_BASE). Set it only to override that:
# "/landing-media/" reads the gitignored local copy in public/landing-media/; another https:// folder or path on
# this site reads that instead; "off" (or anything that isn't https:// or a path) shows the poster as a still, no
# Play, and the three panels drop their links to the film.
# Inlined at BUILD time like every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value: a change on Vercel needs a redeploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MEDIA_BASE=/landing-media/

# Cloudflare R2 (post video objects; key prefix is still clips/ — legacy name). R2 → Overview → Account ID; create bucket + API token with Object Read & Write.
# Server-only — do not use NEXT_PUBLIC_* for these.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=YOUR_CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=YOUR_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=YOUR_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
R2_BUCKET_NAME=YOUR_BUCKET_NAME

# Resend (transactional: .edu verification, password reset, notifications). Server-only.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_YOUR_API_KEY

# Verified-domain sender (Resend → Domains). Required to send password reset + .edu verification.
RESEND_FROM=Vibe <noreply@updates.yourdomain.com>

# Waitlist emails allowed in any trailing 24 hours, counted from email_sends, as TWO separate allowances so the
# public form can never use up the founders' sends: WAITLIST_EMAIL_DAILY_CAP counts access-code emails (default 40),
# WAITLIST_CONFIRM_DAILY_CAP counts the form's confirm emails (default 30; each network also gets at most 10 a day).
# Why: Resend's free tier is 100 emails a day for the whole account, and Supabase Auth's own sign-up mail and the
# password-reset / school-email codes spend the same 100. Raise both after upgrading Resend. Server-only.
# Locally, with RESEND_API_KEY blank, waitlist emails are not sent: the dev server prints one
# "[waitlist-email:dev]" line per email (kind, masked address, link, and the code) instead.
WAITLIST_EMAIL_DAILY_CAP=40
WAITLIST_CONFIRM_DAILY_CAP=30

# Vercel Cron (vercel.json "crons"): Vercel sends "Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>" with each cron call, and
# /api/cron/waitlist-purge (the daily waitlist retention purge: every entry goes 38 days after it joined, inside the
# promised 40) refuses
# anything else. Unset or under 16 characters = every call refused, so the daily purge never runs. Set it on Vercel
# (Production), a random string: `openssl rand -hex 32`. Server-only; not needed locally.
CRON_SECRET=

# Sentry (Settings → Projects → Client Keys → DSN). Needed on client + server; use NEXT_PUBLIC_* as per Sentry Next.js SDK.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://YOUR_KEY@YOUR_ORG.ingest.sentry.io/YOUR_PROJECT_ID

# Stripe (Vibe+ payments). All three are server-only: never NEXT_PUBLIC_*, never in client code or a commit.
# NEVER set any of them on Vercel Preview. Preview shares the production Supabase database, so a preview
# checkout would write real billing rows. On Vercel, tick Production only, as a Sensitive variable.
#
# Locally: a TEST key only (sk_test_… or rk_test_…) from a Stripe sandbox, in .env.development.local,
# which `next dev` reads first. `node scripts/stripe-setup.mjs` then creates the Vibe+ product, its two
# prices (lookup keys vibe_plus_monthly / vibe_plus_yearly) and the Customer Portal settings in that sandbox.
# Production: a RESTRICTED live key (rk_live_…), never the full secret key, with only these permissions:
#   Checkout Sessions: Write   create; also covers list and expire, which the checkout route uses
#   Customers: Write           create at first checkout; delete when someone deletes their Vibe account
#   Customer portal: Write     portal sessions, and finding the Vibe+ portal configuration
#   Subscriptions: Read        retrieve before every entitlement write; also covers subscriptions.list
#   Prices: Read               find the two prices by lookup key
#   Invoices: Read             re-fetch an invoice event to find its subscription
#   Charges: Read              a dispute names only its charge, and the charge names the customer
#   Events: Read               optional; no code calls the Events API today
# That key cannot run scripts/stripe-setup.mjs (no Products or Prices write), on purpose. A live setup run
# uses a separate short-lived key with Products, Prices and Customer portal write. Delete it after the run,
# and never put it on Vercel.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=YOUR_STRIPE_TEST_KEY

# Signing secret (whsec_…) for POST /api/billing/webhook. Every event is checked against it before anything
# happens. Locally: any whsec_ value works when you replay sandbox events with a signed test header, or use
# the one `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/billing/webhook` prints (Stripe CLI).
# Production: from the Dashboard endpoint (Developers → Webhooks), which must
#   * point at https://www.connectvibe.app/api/billing/webhook, www included. The apex connectvibe.app
#     answers with a 308 redirect (next.config.ts), and Stripe does not follow redirects.
#   * use API version 2026-08-26.dahlia, the version the SDK is pinned to and the code reads.
#   * send exactly these events:
#       checkout.session.completed, checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded,
#       checkout.session.async_payment_failed, customer.subscription.created,
#       customer.subscription.updated, customer.subscription.deleted, customer.subscription.paused,
#       customer.subscription.resumed, invoice.paid, invoice.payment_failed, charge.refunded,
#       charge.dispute.created, customer.deleted
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=YOUR_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET

# Vibe+ checkout switch. Exactly `true` turns on Subscribe and checkout; anything else, or unset, is off.
# It also needs STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, or billing stays off: without the webhook,
# Vibe would take the first payment and then miss every renewal, failed card and cancellation.
# Manage subscription (the Stripe portal) works with this off, so a subscriber can always cancel.
# PRODUCTION: leave UNSET until the LLC's EIN and bank account exist AND the Terms with subscription wording
# are published (Franky, 2026-09-22).
# BILLING_ENABLED=true

# Push notifications: one pipeline for browsers (Web Push) and the App Store / Google Play apps (FCM).
# EVERY push value below is PRODUCTION ONLY. NEVER set any of them on Vercel Preview: Preview shares the production
# database, so a preview holding them could buzz real students' phones from unreviewed code. The code refuses to
# push anywhere but production and `next dev` even if one is copied over by mistake (src/lib/push/config.ts).
# Locally: a SEPARATE VAPID pair and a dev Firebase project's account in .env.development.local, against the LOCAL
# Supabase copy only. Every line here is commented out with no value on purpose: the repo is public, and a
# copyable placeholder would be one paste away from a real key. Check a deploy at /api/health/push (admins only).
#
# Switch. Exactly `true` turns push on; anything else, or unset, is off (no queries, no sends).
# PUSH_ENABLED=true
#
# Who gets push while it's on: a comma list of user ids (the founders' test), or `*` for everyone.
# UNSET OR BLANK IS NOBODY, so going public is a deliberate `*`. Narrowing the list stops pushes at once.
# PUSH_ALLOWLIST=
#
# Web Push (VAPID). Generate the pair ONCE with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys` and keep it in the founders'
# password manager. NEVER ROTATE THE PAIR: every browser subscription is bound to the public key, so a new pair
# silently kills every subscription until each student turns notifications on again.
# The public key is public (browsers subscribe with it) and is built into the page, so a change needs a redeploy.
# The private key is server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_*: Vercel Production only, Sensitive.
# The subject is how push services reach us: `mailto:` an address on connectvibe.app, or https://www.connectvibe.app.
# NEVER localhost: Apple refuses it (403 BadJwtToken) while Chrome accepts it, so it would fail on iPhones only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=
#
# FCM (both store apps; Firebase hands iPhone pushes to Apple). The service account's whole JSON file, base64'd
# with a pipe so the file never lands in the repo folder: `base64 -i ~/Downloads/<file>.json | pbcopy`, then
# paste into Vercel (Production only, Sensitive) and delete the download. Use a service account that holds ONLY
# the "Firebase Cloud Messaging API Admin" role, never the default firebase-adminsdk account. No sample value
# here: a key-shaped example is exactly what secret scanners block a push for.
# FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_B64=

# Club chat v1 (`chat_v2`): the new Messages inbox, club rooms' screens and cards, behind a per-person switch
# (src/lib/chat/flag.ts, src/lib/chat/flag-server.ts). The database side (rooms, the Board rule) is NOT behind it.
# EVERY value below is PRODUCTION ONLY and server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_*. NEVER set any of them on Vercel
# Preview: Preview runs against the production database, so a preview holding them would open unreviewed screens
# on real clubs. Locally: in .env.development.local, against the LOCAL Supabase copy only. Every line here is
# commented out with no value on purpose. On Vercel a changed value applies from the next deploy.
# A screen learns `chat_v2` from GET /api/me/features; the desktop pages (/messages, /campus) also receive
# `chat_desktop` as a server prop.
#
# Switch. Exactly `true` turns the feature on at all; anything else, or unset, is off for everyone.
# It only counts on the live site (VERCEL_ENV=production) and in `next dev`; on a Vercel Preview build it does nothing.
# CHAT_V2_ENABLED=
#
# Who gets it while it's on: a comma list of user ids (the founders' test), or `*` for everyone.
# UNSET OR BLANK IS NOBODY, so going public is a deliberate `*`.
# The star must be the whole value; a star inside a list is ignored (the server log says so once).
# CHAT_V2_ALLOWLIST=
#
# Whole clubs: a comma list of club (org) ids, not handles. Every current member of a listed club is in, for as
# long as they are a member. An entry that is not an id is ignored (the server log says so once).
# CHAT_V2_CLUBS=
#
# Messages on desktop (`chat_desktop`): the new Messages page on a window 900px wide or more, behind its OWN
# per-person switch (src/lib/chat/flag.ts, src/lib/chat/flag-desktop-server.ts), so the phone never waits for it.
# The same three warnings as `chat_v2` above. (1) PRODUCTION ONLY and server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# (2) NEVER on Vercel Preview: Preview runs against the production database. (3) Locally: in
# .env.development.local, against the LOCAL Supabase copy only. On Vercel a changed value applies from the next deploy.
# It never widens `chat_v2`: a person gets desktop Messages only when BOTH switches are on for them, because the
# routes the desktop page reads answer 404 without `chat_v2`. There is no clubs list for desktop.
#
# Switch. Exactly `true` turns desktop Messages on at all; anything else, or unset, is off for everyone.
# It only counts on the live site (VERCEL_ENV=production) and in `next dev`; on a Vercel Preview build it does nothing.
# CHAT_DESKTOP_ENABLED=
#
# Who gets it while it's on: a comma list of user ids, or `*` for everyone who already has `chat_v2`.
# UNSET OR BLANK IS NOBODY. The star must be the whole value; a star inside a list is ignored.
# CHAT_DESKTOP_ALLOWLIST=

# School calendars on Campus ("What's the vibe tonight?"). Indianapolis: IU Indy home games, IU Indianapolis
# Student Affairs and Featured events. Bloomington (since Oct 19, 2026): IU Athletics home games, IU Bloomington
# Student Life (group 76) and Featured (group 341). Each campus shows only its own.
# ON BY DEFAULT: leave this UNSET and every calendar shows. Server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# It is a kill switch, Production only, and a changed value applies from the next deploy:
#   true (or 1, yes, on, *, all)      every school calendar off, both campuses (the school parts vanish)
#   iu-bloomington                    every Bloomington calendar off (a campus id; `indianapolis` works too)
#   iub-athletics                     only that calendar off; keys: athletics, iu-student-affairs, iu-featured
#                                     (Indianapolis), iub-athletics, iub-student-life, iub-featured (Bloomington)
#   iub-athletics,iu-featured         a comma list of keys and campus ids: those off
#   unset, false, 0, no, off          on
# A word the build doesn't know (a typo, or a key from a newer build) turns NOTHING off and logs one warning
# (Oct 19, 2026: it used to turn every campus off, so a Bloomington name could hide Indianapolis). Check the
# screens after setting it. Only a value that names nothing at all (",") still turns everything off.
# Faster, with no deploy: the `public.app_settings` row `school_events_off` (true, or a JSON array of the same
# words, like ["iub-athletics"]) turns them off within about 30 s. That row is a production write; the SQL and
# the rules are in src/lib/school-events/switch.ts. Shipping writes no row.
# BEFORE ROLLING PRODUCTION BACK past Oct 19, 2026 (9117dc6 or older): if that row holds a Bloomington word,
# delete it (those builds show no Bloomington anyway). They read a word they don't know as "every calendar off",
# so Indy would vanish too. An instant rollback keeps the old deploy's env; only a fresh redeploy reads this one.
# SCHOOL_EVENTS_OFF=true
#
# Development only (`next dev`; ignored everywhere else): read the calendars from src/lib/school-events/fixtures/
# instead of the live sites, so working on Campus never hammers them. `1` reads the fixtures; `fail` makes every
# calendar fail, to see the screens with the school part down. Pair it with `?tonight_now=<ISO>` on /campus.
# SCHOOL_EVENTS_FIXTURES=1

# Optional — show the global `/feed` app route + left nav item. Omit or set to anything
# other than `true` during campus-only phase so `/feed` redirects to `/campus` and
# campus posts are not implied to be “global” until you add explicit visibility.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_GLOBAL_FEED=true

# Optional — CI / production builds: upload source maps (never commit the token).
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug
# SENTRY_PROJECT=vibe
